  (text "SAO++ power select: the switch common feeds the LEDs. Position 1 = badge 3.3 V, position 2 = OFF (pin 2 unconnected), position 3 = coin cell." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 38.1 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "cd90d41e-f334-57ff-9d60-d5f95b33900c"))
  (text "The badge supply and the coin cell sit on separate switch contacts and are never connected to each other." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 41.91 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "f1f91545-0790-5f2b-8887-316eeee0a931"))
  (text "LED-only board: SDA, SCL, GPIO1 and GPIO2 are not connected, so no series diode is needed on the cell (see docs/standard.md section 3)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 45.72 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "2ba0bece-d5ee-505f-9cce-791e9de94a44"))
  (text "D1 = right eye, D2 = left eye (as seen from the front). The 2018-era original had two 5 mm LEDs straight on the badge 3.3 V with no resistor." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 147.32 96.52 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d76bb3d5-cee4-5e28-9209-6c8a978193c4"))
  (text "One 1.3k resistor per white LED: about 0.45 mA each on badge power, about 0.2 mA each on a fresh cell." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 147.32 100.33 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b2816b58-090a-55fd-85aa-990f19c11c64"))
